      "source_hint": "pulumi awsx",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/guides/clouds/aws/elb.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L262-263",
      "text": "A target group is automatically created for each listener that doesn't override the default action in the AWSx ELB component.",
      "type": "behavior",
      "source_hint": "pulumi awsx",
      "confidence": "high",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/guides/clouds/aws/elb.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L262-263",
      "text": "An AWSx target group can be used to load balance any number of targets, including EC2 instances, ECS services, or arbitrary IPs.",
      "type": "feature",
      "source_hint": "pulumi awsx",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/guides/clouds/aws/elb.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L264-266",
      "text": "You can create a target group manually by defining a `defaultTargetGroup` on the load balancer directly.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "pulumi awsx",
      "confidence": "high",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/guides/clouds/aws/elb.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L264-266",
      "text": "You can create a target group manually by creating a `TargetGroupAttachment` resource.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "pulumi awsx",
      "confidence": "high",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/guides/clouds/aws/elb.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L268-270",
      "text": "The `deregistrationDelay` target group property specifies the amount of time for ELB to wait before changing the state of a load balancer from draining to unused.",
      "type": "api-surface",
